1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
I nearly bought the stolen tools back
from myself. That's how tired I was.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:12,056
Jason had hidden our cash inside a tool
chest. By sunrise, the refinery

3
00:00:12,056 --> 00:00:14,000
had impounded all three boxes.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:19,353
An auction stamp appeared on each
inventory slip. The ink smeared on mine

5
00:00:19,353 --> 00:00:21,000
before anybody touched it.

6
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:25,529
That meant the paperwork came first.
Whoever stamped the slips hadn't

7
00:00:25,529 --> 00:00:28,000
opened the chests or looked inside.

8
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:33,765
I asked Jason for the money envelope. He
handed me an empty one and

9
00:00:33,765 --> 00:00:35,000
stopped looking nervous.

10
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:40,158
We'd switched the labels while the ink
dried. Our chest was now listed as

11
00:00:40,158 --> 00:00:42,000
damaged equipment, scheduled for
disposal.

12
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,789
We collected it at the scrap gate, paid
the disposal charge, and recovered

13
00:00:46,789 --> 00:00:49,000
the cash beneath its false bottom.

14
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:54,526
I lost twenty dollars on the fee. Jason
called it expensive. I told him to

15
00:00:54,526 --> 00:00:56,000
buy his own money.
